    "created_at": "2016-06-03T16:40:45Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-03T16:40:45Z",
    "body": "> This might be slightly OT, but I believe ES6 prevents multiple calls to super.\n\nIt only sort of does. It calls the super-constructor twice, then throws an error when it tries to set `this` to the second result. So you still need to guard against the possibility in HTMLElement.\n\nI tend to agree with @rniwa that keeping them separate is better. Synchronous element creation via `new X()` must necessarily be different from create-then-upgrade. I think `createElement()` should match `new X()`, not create-then-upgrade, because `new X()` has fewer quirks.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
